> Starting Strategy

As others have pointed out, the exploration methods all sound similar, 
except for the pet part.

> I find this a delicate balancing act and recommend you pick a
> strategy that fits your level of risk taking and general comfort level

The primary goal of exploration is to improve the character by finding 
items and locations (Minetown, Sokoban, altars, shops, fountains).

Finding and hunting down monsters is not an important goal:
- Their equipment, if they have any, is typically junk.
- Most corpses don't give intrinsics.
- The nutrition is nice, but food is everywhere.
- Gaining levels is a net benefit, but not as much as obtaining good 
items, and can be risky if your AC doesn't keep pace (interestingly, this 
is less true with the recommended classes, who get the speed intrinsic at 
level 7, and typically gain boatloads of HP from their 18 CON).
- Fighting monsters is much more dangerous than finding items.
- Most importantly, no matter where you go or what you do, you'll find 
monsters, because the game generates them constantly.  There is no reason 
to hunt them down, because they will be hunting you down.

Mapping every nook and cranny of every level is not a goal.  Thorough 
exploration of the early levels is needed to find shops and the Mines 
stairs, but as you go deeper, exploration becomes less important.  There 
_might_ be an unexplored 3x4 room in the far corner of DL8, and if it 
exists it _might_ contain an item, but there are guaranteed to be many 
rooms on DL9, and some of them will contain items.   

