> Get teleport control by eating the Wizard of Yendor

That's a long time to wait for TC, and there's a nasty luck penalty.  The 
normal way to obtain TC is from a ring, while tinning or eating every 
tengu generated, even the peaceful ones.  TC is a powerful intrinsic that 
should be a high priority in the mid-game.  If no TC ring has been 
generated by the post-Castle stage, c?G for tengu is very worthwhile.  
Wizards and Monks get TC for free at XL17.

The Eye doesn't do level teleport, but something similar, though better. 
TC isn't relevant to the use of the Eye.

^T requires teleportitis (easily obtained) and XL12.  This costs exactly 
20 energy.  Without teleportitis, ^T will attempt to use the teleport 
away spell, but this is not recommended, because it costs 30 mana and 
typically has high failure rates.  

If the player has enough mana (the Eye), ^T will burn through nutrition 
fast enough that the food warning is actually appropriate.  But that 
isn't a reason to limit the use of ^T, but a reason to carry a decent 
stack of food/C/K rations.

