> After MC, there is no clear consensus on which cloak is better.

In the early and mid game, the choice of a cloak is dictated mainly by 
what the RNG provides, and then by the particular needs of the character, 
which will change over the course of the game.  But there is a rough 
hierarchy:

Cloak of magic resistance is mandatory if it is the only source of MR.  
Otherwise it's just a basic MC3 cloak.  Because of bones files, it is the 
second most common non-mundane cloak.

Elven cloak is the most common MC3 cloak, and the default choice if 
[MR isn't available or desired.  Enough elves will eventually show up 
that you have a good chance at +1 or better.  The stealth will only be 
relevant to some classes.

Robes are great if your character knows a good combat spell, and has a 
good casting stat, and enough mana regen to make it worthwhile.  This 
isn't common pre-Castle, but a robe still provides 2 points of AC and 
MC3, so it will sometimes be the best cloak available.

Displacement is better than invisibility, but they are both good choices 
in the early game.  One can get by with "only" MC2 for a long time.  By 
the time the need for MC3 becomes pressing, the player has likely 
obtained intrinsic invisibility anyway, so they can be tossed aside 
without regrets.

Cloak of protection: Two points of AC isn't as good as the special 
abilities of the other cloaks

> Some want the oilskin cloak to avoid drowning by krakens.

Some people are awful.

Honorable mention to the apron, which makes itself obsolete almost right 
away. 

Only two cloaks are, IMO, powerful enough to be "worth" a wish.  But most 
of the time wishing [MR is not the best way to obtain the intrinsic, and 
the game guarantees two robes.

> Early in the game - if you do not need to cast spells, mithril (elven or
> dwarven) is an excellent choice.

The _best_ choice, unless an early wish is available.  It's rustproof, 
too.

If you do need to cast spells, you're stuck with studded leather; crystal 
plate is rare, and too heavy.

> The Protection Racket

The racket is a bad idea for most (some say all) characters, and 
certainly all newbies.  AC:1 is obtainable with normal play, just not as 
quickly as with the racket.

